        "original_id": "cf7218c9-aa7b-5da5-8a67-8283a6e2fd4a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jim Thompson, Theodore H. White\n- Works: Savage Night\n- Roles: author, screenwriter, political journalist, historian\n- Topics: hardboiled crime fiction, wartime reporting from China, U.S. presidential elections\n\nFacts:\n- James Myers Thompson was born on September 27, 1906, and he was an American author and screenwriter known for hardboiled crime fiction.\n- Theodore Harold White was born on May 6, 1915, and he was an American political journalist and historian known for wartime reporting from China.\n- Savage Night is a 1953 novel by thriller writer Jim Thompson.\n- Theodore H. White wrote accounts of the 1960, 1964, 1968, 1972, 1976, and 1980 U.S. presidential elections.\n- James Myers Thompson died on April 7, 1977.\n- Theodore Harold White died on May 15, 1986.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
